    "text": "Let $x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\in \\mathbb{R}^2$ be such that no circle whose centre is one of the $x_i$ contains three other points. Are there at least $ (1+c)\\frac{n}{2} $ distinct distances determined between the $x_i$, for some constant $c>0$ and all $n$ sufficiently large?",
